WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.779
I'm truly glad to be able to come to you today
and give you just an overview of some good

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:12.919
news about the virus, and of course we'll
discuss the continued challenges. And there's

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:17.330
lots of bad news. So I'm not pretending it
doesn't exist, but I want to give everybody

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.540
some updates that will give us some hope that
we're starting to move in the right direction,

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:28.500
despite the obvious challenges and an unconscionable
death that still are ahead of us. So first

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.969
of all, the I H M E model, which is one of
the top models currently being monitored and

00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:41.789
updated daily, has moved the peak in terms
of deaths in the United States up from April

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:49.460
16th to April 12th. That's now just four days
away. The peak day previously was expected

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:56.140
to have 3000 deaths in one day in the United
States. That number has dropped by almost

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:03.140
a third to twenty two hundred. Still horrifying.
But one third lower than it was expected to

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:09.250
be. Now, importantly, the peak is not really
a single day. It's more of a plateau. And

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.610
that plateau is expected to run from today.
We are essentially in that peak plateau right

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:21.150
now from today until close to the end of the
month. But the latest prediction is that deaths

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:27.500
will start to decline in the United States
just four days from now. Roughly the peak

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.250
is going to come on a different day in different
states, California, New York, Massachusetts,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.430
other places. But that is in general good
news. We are closer to getting over the hump

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:43.680
than we previously believed. Number two, another
bit of good news. Once the data from the last

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:50.710
few days was added to the model, the expected
death toll of this first wave of Corona virus

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:57.040
has dropped to 60000. Now, that's a crazy
number of people. But last week, the model

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.670
predicted 93000 deaths in the first wave in
the U.S. Earlier this week, the model predicted

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:10.069
82000. That number has now dropped an additional
sort of 27 ish percent to sixty thousand deaths,

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:17.730
a terrible number, but a reduction of almost
50 percent since the or 35 ish, 35, 40 percent

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:23.540
since the prediction was 93000. Now, why do
I keep saying the first wave really important

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:29.510
to understand this. Some models have a death
toll prediction. That is for what are expected

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:34.599
to be three waves of infection. This model
is looking just that, the first wave right

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:39.689
now, doctors and scientists believe we are
currently in wave one. We will fall off of

00:02:39.689 --> 00:02:46.049
that wave in May, June, July in the fall.
There will be another peak, which is wave

00:02:46.049 --> 00:02:52.650
two. And then in 2021, there would be a third
wave, which is wave three. Hopefully by then

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.469
we would be well-prepared to really mitigate,
but that remains to be seen. This wave may

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:02.439
end up with a far lower death toll than we
thought, which would be because of what we

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:06.849
are doing. I'll get to that in a moment. One
other bit of good news. AV, again, I told

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:11.989
you about AV again weeks ago, maybe a month
ago. It's one of the possible treatments that's

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:17.950
being explored for Corona virus. We are now
starting a clinical trial of Afghan Japanese

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:24.109
drug right here in Boston. Trump won't stop
talking about chloroquine. Chloroquine has

00:03:24.109 --> 00:03:30.019
some promise, but recent studies are not super
auspicious. I previously told you about AB

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:35.919
again, it is showing promise and it's going
to be tested in Boston across a few hospitals.

00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:40.669
Another bit of really good news is that New
York hospitals have been starting to discharge

00:03:40.669 --> 00:03:45.900
more patients than are being that then are
having intakes that are being brought in over

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:52.029
the last few days. New York is a huge hotspot
right now. 35 percent of all official cases

00:03:52.029 --> 00:03:56.909
in the country are in New York State. If you
include New Jersey, New York, New Jersey have

00:03:56.909 --> 00:04:02.719
47 percent of all of the official cases. It's
a very good sign that things are starting

00:04:02.719 --> 00:04:09.290
to level out there. Other states have to keep
it up in terms of distancing. Now, remember,

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:14.590
anytime that things look better than expected,
a whole bunch of people will say, we told

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:20.919
you you were overreacting. We can stop the
social distancing. This is a virus. It spreads

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:26.919
virally. That's where the word comes from.
If what you are doing works, it should feel

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:31.729
like you overreacted. If you're doing the
right thing, it should feel like you're doing

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:37.150
too much for the level of spread because you
have to be ahead of the curve. Anti-vaxxers

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:42.009
will often say we don't really need vaccines
because measles is so rare. A lot of these

00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:48.580
conditions are so rare. They are rare because
of the success of the vaccines. If we reduce

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:55.090
deaths, as the model suggests we are doing,
it's because we were staying home and closing

00:04:55.090 --> 00:05:01.340
things down, not despite it. It's still going
to be tough. We currently. About 13000 deaths

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.800
in the U.S., if we believe the model and we
will end up somewhere just under 61000, what

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.360
that means is that 80 percent of the death
is ahead of us, mostly in the next four to

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:17.979
six weeks. This is really tough. Let's stay
in this. Keep pushing on treatment. Keep moving

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:22.360
the vaccine forward. Keep being responsible.
And by the end of the week, I'll be able to

00:05:22.360 --> 00:06:45.450
further update you about where the numbers
are.

